From 6351d9430324a778b5140d7f200553b28faad03a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Leon <leon@mbp.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:07:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] fix(server): stop re-emitting Claude content blocks that
 were already streamed

The Claude Code SDK sends one assistant message per content block, all sharing
the API message id. The timeline assembler treated each one as a cumulative
snapshot, so when a second thinking or text block arrived after its stream
deltas, the text no longer prefix-matched the accumulated text, the emitted
counter reset, and the block was emitted a second time.

Merge absolute assistant text instead: a growing snapshot replaces the
accumulated text, a block already present at the end is treated as streamed,
and any other block is appended. The merged text always extends what was
emitted, so the emitted counters never reset.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
